LMN 1
title: Morning Bread
artist: Shiori examples
tempo: 156
time: 6/8
key: F major
mood: sunny, bustling, teasing; flour in the air at five in the morning

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// HINATA'S THEME. A 6/8 bakery jig: acoustic guitar, accordion, wooden flute,
// hand claps and upright bass.
//
// TEMPO  tempo 156 is quarter notes per minute, so the dotted quarter (the
//        felt 6/8 beat) is 104, as the brief asks (LMN-Spec 2.10).
//
// THE KITCHEN CHORD  Fadd9 voiced F3 A3 C4 G4 (the guitar's open Fadd9
//        shape). Hinata's beads "ring together in a chord, always the same
//        warm chord, like a kitchen". The guitar picks it in the first bar,
//        the accordion holds it under the tune, and the song ends on it.
//
// HINATA'S TUNE  (the A strain, 16 bars; quoted in suzu_song and paper_lantern)
//   The head climbs the kitchen chord and lands on its ninth:
//     C5 F5 A5 G5 (four notes, all from F-A-C-G), then A G F C.
//   Bars 5-6 put the same gesture on Bb (F Bb D, landing on C6).
//   Bar 7 runs E F G toward the A that would make the chord warm again...
//
// THE TIRED BAR  ...and in bar 8 it does not get there. The flute freezes on
//   G5 and the harmony underneath goes from Fadd9 to F minor add9 (F3 Ab3 C4
//   G4): the kitchen chord with one note gone flat. The claps stop, the guitar
//   strums once, the bass holds. Nothing resolves it. Bar 9 simply starts the
//   tune again, grinning. ("For one second her face goes flat and white and
//   far away... Then she's grinning again.") The same bar returns in every A
//   section. Only at bar 16 does the run finally reach A5, over Fadd9.
//
// FORM  79 bars of 6/8 at q=156, about 1:31. The song ends on the kitchen
//       chord held by the accordion; the Intro begins on the same chord on the
//       guitar, so the loop comes round without a bump.
//   Intro   4  guitar picks the kitchen chord; accordion breathes it in; bass,
//              claps and a flute run-up join
//   A1     16  flute: Hinata's tune. Accordion holds the chords, guitar picks
//   B      16  the tease: the accordion sings a falling line in threes against
//              the bass's twos (hemiola), with a cheeky II7 (G7, B natural);
//              the flute joins in sixths, then leads a chromatic shimmy
//              (A G# A, G F# G) with the accordion a third below
//   A2     16  the accordion takes Hinata's tune; the flute answers in thirds
//              below in the second half
//   C       8  the soft Hinata ("You'd look nice in a hat"): the head slowed to
//              half speed over Bbmaj7, no claps; claps fill back in
//   A3     16  everyone: flute tune, accordion in thirds, strummed guitar,
//              walking bass, clap-along on both beats. The tired bar still
//              comes, the same as before
//   Outro   3  the head once more, softly, and the kitchen chord held
//
// HARMONY (A strain)
//   Fadd9 | Fadd9 | Gm7 | C7 | Bb(add9) | Am7 | Gm7 C7 | Fm(add9) |
//   Fadd9 | Fadd9 | Gm7 | C7 | Bb(add9) | Am7 | Gm7 C7 | Fadd9    |
// HARMONY (B strain)
//   Bb(add9) | Fadd9 | Gm7 | C7 | Bb(add9) | Fadd9 | Dm7 | G7 |
//   Bb(add9) | Fadd9 | Gm7 | C7 | Dm7      | Gm7   | F/C | C7 |
// HARMONY (C)
//   Bbmaj7 | Bbmaj7 | F/A | F/A | Gm7 | Am7 | Bbmaj7 | C7 |
//
// Accordion voicings stay inside F3-A4 and move by step from the kitchen
// chord: Fadd9 F3 A3 C4 G4 · Gm7 F3 Bb3 D4 G4 · C7 E3 Bb3 C4 G4 ·
// Bb(add9) F3 Bb3 C4 D4 · Am7 E3 A3 C4 G4 · Fm(add9) F3 Ab3 C4 G4.
// (The C section keeps a dreamier Bbmaj7, F3 Bb3 D4 A4.)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

track flute      flute            vol=80 pan=-12 reverb=30
track accordion  accordion        vol=60 pan=22  reverb=26
track guitar     acoustic_guitar  vol=60 pan=-28 reverb=22
track bass       upright_bass     vol=76 pan=4   reverb=12
track claps      percussion       vol=48 pan=14  reverb=28

section Intro bars=4
guitar      | !mp F3e A3e C4e G4e C4e A3e | % | G3e Bb3e D4e F4e D4e Bb3e | C3e G3e Bb3e E4e Bb3e G3e |
accordion   | R | !pp [F3 A3 C4 G4]h. | !p [F3 Bb3 D4 G4]h. | [E3 Bb3 C4 G4]h. |
bass        | R | R | !mp G1q. D2q. | C2q. D2q E2e |
claps.clap  | R | R | !mp ... x.. | ... x.x |
flute       | R | R | R | rq. !mp G4e A4e Bb4e |

